. Provide just the brief, no extra text. Let's try a different approach - maybe the user wants me to just output the brief without the function call? But the system prompt says \\\"Always call read_note for the city first.\\\" So I need to call read_note, but then what? The user says \\\"Reply with the brief only.\\\" So after calling read_note, I should output the brief only.\\n\\nBut the user also says \\\"Reply with the brief only.\\\" So maybe I should just output the two-sentence brief as requested, without any reasoning or apologies.\\n\\nActually, wait. The user message is a bit confusing.. Reply with the brief only.\"}]}, {\"role\": \"assistant\", \"parts\": [{\"type\": \"tool_call\", \"name\": \"'read_note'\", \"arguments\": \"'{\\\"city\\\":\\\"Lisbon\\\"}'\", \"id\": \"call-88737422-d848-4c40-ab3a-2971b4013737\"}]}, {\"role\": \"tool\", \"parts\": [{\"type\": \"text\", \"content\": \"Lisbon is the capital of Portugal and lies on the Tagus estuary.\"}]}]" ;
